Cell["\<\
Now, replace H using the tt-equation. H\[CloseCurlyQuote] and H\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]\[CloseCurlyQuote] are obtained from the rr-equation.

Begin by substituting the expression for \
H\[CloseCurlyQuote]\[CloseCurlyQuote], since it contains H\[CloseCurlyQuote]. \
Next, substitute the expression for H\[CloseCurlyQuote], which still contains \
(H). Finally, substitute the expression for H, yielding an equation written \
entirely in terms of K and its derivatives (upto second order). \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9894535935751276`*^9, 3.9894536137170305`*^9}, {
